<title>RUSSIA: Rouble pressured by c.bank selling, clients, T-bills.</title>
<headline>Rouble pressured by c.bank selling, clients, T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rouble eased on Thursday and dealers said higher supply could be due to central bank selling earlier this week, client orders and funds flowing in from the Treasury bill market.</p>
<p> roubles/dollar	Mar 13 midday  Mar 13 early   Mar 12 close</p>
<p> today settlement    5,697-98	 5,697-99	 5,686-88</p>
<p> tomorrow settlement 5,702-04	 5,702-04	 5,697-99</p>
<p> overnight credit (%)   10-15	    35-40	    60-80</p>
<p>			   Mar 13				Mar 12</p>
<p> central bank	  5,692/5,708			 5,691/5,707</p>
<p> MICEX		   5,701				 5,699</p>
<p>&quot;Rouble supply is higher today as the central bank was buying dollars actively for the last two days. Some money could also be coming in after the T-bill auctions,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers said client orders to buy dollars could also be pressuring the rouble.</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
